# Section Navigation

## Source of truth

- Section index and ArrowUp/Down handling live in `App.jsx` via `useSectionNav`.
- Do not add local `keydown` handlers for ArrowUp/ArrowDown/PageUp/PageDown anywhere else.
- Cursor position must not matter: keys work over any card, including scrollable ones.

## Key behavior

- ArrowDown / PageDown → next section.
- ArrowUp / PageUp → previous section.
- Handler: `window` capture phase, `preventDefault` + `stopPropagation` so the browser never scrolls a card.
- Exception: focused `input` / `textarea` / `select` / `contentEditable` (caret / form use).
- While `body.nav-paused` (e.g. project modal), do not change section; still block default ↑/↓ scroll.
- Enforce nav lock for the morph duration so rapid keys cannot skip mid-animation.

## Cards and scroll

- Cards may scroll with wheel/touch only.
- Never use ArrowUp/Down to scroll `.thin-scroll` / overflow areas.
- Left/Right may still drive horizontal carousels (Projects); they must not steal ↑/↓.

## Other nav

- Section slider and in-content CTAs call `jumpTo` / `goTo` from the same App-owned state.
- Wheel on the main canvas shows the “use arrow keys” hint; it does not change sections.
